<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Tippu Tip's State</h1><p class="st-meta">1870 CE – 1894 CE (approx.) · capital Kasongo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The commercial empire of the Zanzibari trader Tippu Tip on the upper Congo, built on ivory and slaves and broken by the Congo Free State.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tippu-tip">Hamed bin Muhammad al-Murjebi</a>, called Tippu Tip, was a Swahili-Arab trader from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sultanate-of-zanzibar">Zanzibar</a> who led caravans deep into the interior from the 1860s. In the 1870s he established himself in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manyema">Manyema</a> on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lualaba">Lualaba</a>, making Kasongo the centre of a domain of trading posts, allied chiefs and armed followers.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The state was a commercial network rather than a kingdom: armed bands collected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and captives, plantations of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> and other crops fed the settlements, and goods moved east to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sultanate-of-zanzibar">Zanzibar</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tippu-tip">Tippu Tip</a> helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-morton-stanley">Henry Morton Stanley</a> down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lualaba">Lualaba</a> in 1876, and in 1887 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/congo-free-state">Congo Free State</a> appointed him governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boyoma-falls">Stanley Falls</a> district.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tippu-tip">Tippu Tip</a> retired to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sultanate-of-zanzibar">Zanzibar</a> in 1890. War broke out between the Free State and the Swahili-Arab traders in 1892, Kasongo fell in 1893, and by 1894 the state had been destroyed, its lands absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/congo-free-state">Congo Free State</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tippu-tips-state.jpg" alt="Tippu Tip's State" width="320" height="238"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Sultanate_of_Zanzibar.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1870 CE – 1894 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kasongo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tippu Tip, Sefu bin Hamed</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Swahili, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kasongo, Manyema Arab state</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1882&amp;focus=tippu-tips-state" aria-label="Tippu Tip's State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5419 2344 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tippu Tip's State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5739 2600L6086 2664M5739 2600L5362 2652"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6086 2664h0M5362 2652h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5739 2600h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5739 2600h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kasongo. <a href="/atlas?year=1882&amp;focus=tippu-tips-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

